# N2/P7 Results — Two C-Backed 64-bit Annotation Words

## Executive result

P7 preserves P4-P6's propagated-signature mathematics exactly, and the lowering-only speed signal remains a clear PASS on Gate-P. However, the hypothesized construction-time improvement from replacing P6's in-node Python integers with two `array('Q')` buffers **did not occur**. P7 construction is slower than simultaneous P6 and P5, so the preregistered end-to-end signal remains FAIL.

## Gate-P primary endpoints

| comparison | ratio | bootstrap 95% CI |
|---|---:|---:|
| P7 / direct lowering | **0.6671x** | **0.4998-0.8799** |
| P7 / P6 lowering | 0.9714x | 0.9601-0.9823 |
| P7 / P5 lowering | 1.0067x | 0.9913-1.0231 |
| **P7 full pipeline / direct** | **1.3052x** | **1.0940-1.5320** |
| P7 full pipeline / P6 | 1.0390x | 1.0149-1.0614 |
| P7 full pipeline / P5 | 1.0322x | 0.9981-1.0622 |
| **P7 DAG build / direct** | **2.6245x** | **2.4080-2.8309** |
| P7 DAG build / P6 | **1.0723x** | **1.0481-1.0942** |
| P7 DAG build / P5 | **1.0762x** | **1.0461-1.1045** |

Lowering-only PASS: **True**. End-to-end PASS: **False**.

P7 beats direct lowering on 23/36 Gate-P cases and beats direct end-to-end on 6/36.

The workload-weighted complete-pipeline ratio is **1.0039x direct**. This is essentially parity, but remains a secondary endpoint and cannot replace the failed case-balanced preregistered criterion.

## Symbolic work and decision equivalence

P7, P6, and P5 agree exactly on all preregistered symbolic/selector fields. Gate-P totals are:

- demanded selector nodes: **322**;
- demanded propagated candidates: **181**;
- accepted folds: **29**;
- accepted shared folds: **22**;
- consumed folds: **29**;
- propagated-signature nodes: **520**.

Relative to direct, P7 performs:

- multiplications: **0.3360x**;
- pair terms: **0.0984x**;
- evaluated ANF nodes: **0.5415x**;
- peak monomials: **0.8973x**.

Thus the underlying folding mechanism still removes about **90.2%** of pair-product work on this fold-rich workload.

